.TH HYPRPAPER 1 "2026-05-02" "hyprpaper v0.8.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprpaper \- fast, IPC-controlled wallpaper utility for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprpaper
[\fB\-c\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprpaper
is a fast, IPC-controlled wallpaper utility for Hyprland. It reads a
configuration file to set per-monitor wallpapers and supports runtime
control via
.BR hyprctl (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Set a custom config file path. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/hypr/hyprpaper.conf .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable more verbose logging output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print hyprpaper's version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help menu and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is located at
.IR ~/.config/hypr/hyprpaper.conf .
It is not required; hyprpaper can be controlled entirely via IPC.
.SS Wallpaper blocks
Wallpapers are declared in
.B wallpaper
blocks. Multiple blocks may be specified. A block with an empty
.B monitor
field acts as a fallback for monitors that have not been assigned a specific
wallpaper.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
wallpaper {
    monitor   = DP-3
    path      = ~/myFile.jxl
    fit_mode  = cover
}

wallpaper {
    monitor   =
    path      = ~/fallback.jxl
    fit_mode  = cover
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The following options are recognized inside a
.B wallpaper { }
block:
.TP
.B monitor
Monitor ID to target. Leave empty to use this wallpaper as a fallback for
any monitor without a specific assignment.
.TP
.B path
Path to an image file, or a directory containing image files.
Required.
.TP
.B fit_mode
How to display the image. One of
.BR contain ,
.BR cover ,
.BR tile ,
or
.BR fill .
Defaults to
.BR cover .
.TP
.B timeout
Seconds between wallpaper changes when
.B path
is a directory. Defaults to
.BR 30 .
.TP
.B order
Order in which images are shown when
.B path
is a directory. Currently the only supported value is
.BR random .
.TP
.B recursive
Whether to scan subdirectories recursively when
.B path
is a directory. Defaults to
.BR false .
.SS Global options
These options are set outside any
.B wallpaper { }
block.
.TP
.B splash
Render the Hyprland splash over the wallpaper. Boolean, defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.B splash_offset
How far up the splash is displayed. Float, defaults to
.BR 20 .
.TP
.B splash_opacity
Opacity of the splash (0.0\[en]1.0). Float, defaults to
.BR 0.8 .
.TP
.B ipc
Enable IPC support. Boolean, defaults to
.BR true .
.SS Sourcing
Additional files can be included with the
.B source
keyword. Globbing, tilde expansion, and relative paths are supported.
Processing is linear: lines before
.B source
are parsed first.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
source = ~/.config/hypr/hyprpaper.d/*.conf
.fi
.RE
.SH IPC
.B hyprpaper
supports IPC via
.BR hyprctl (1).
To set a wallpaper at runtime:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
hyprctl hyprpaper wallpaper '\fImon\fR, \fIpath\fR[, \fIfit_mode\fR]'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I mon
may be left empty for the fallback target.
.I fit_mode
is optional.
The fallback wallpaper only applies to monitors that have never had a
specific monitor target assigned.
.SH AUTOSTART
To launch hyprpaper automatically with Hyprland, add the following line to
.IR ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf :
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
exec-once = hyprpaper
.fi
.RE
.PP
On Parrot, the default Hyprland configuration starts Hyprpaper and reads
.IR ~/.config/hypr/hyprpaper.conf .
Do not enable the systemd user service separately.
.PP
Outside the Parrot desktop, if Hyprland is started with
.BR uwsm ,
you may alternatively enable the provided systemd user service:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
systemctl --user enable --now hyprpaper.service
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/hyprpaper.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprland (1),
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR hyprpicker (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The Hypr Development team and contributors.
.br
.UR https://github.com/hyprwm/hyprpaper
.UE
